properties.description:
BATCH PROPERTY SETTING: Set multiple properties simultaneously for efficiency. Each property MUST specify exact type and value. CRITICAL: Property names must match exactly (case-sensitive), types must be accurate. Use component_query to inspect property types first!

📝 FORMAT:
{
  "propertyName": {"type": "exactPropertyType", "value": actualValue}
}

🎯 EXAMPLES BY TYPE:
• TEXT: {"string": {"type": "string", "value": "Hello World"}}
• NUMBERS: {"fontSize": {"type": "number", "value": 28}}
• COLORS: {"color": {"type": "color", "value": {"r":255,"g":100,"b":50,"a":255}}}
• BOOLEANS: {"isBold": {"type": "boolean", "value": true}}
• VECTORS: {"anchorPoint": {"type": "vec2", "value": {"x":0.5,"y":1.0}}}
• SIZES: {"contentSize": {"type": "size", "value": {"width":200,"height":80}}}
• NODE REFS: {"player": {"type": "node", "value": "node-uuid-here"}}
• ASSETS: {"bulletPrefab": {"type": "prefab", "value": "prefab-uuid-here"}}
• SPRITES: {"spriteFrame": {"type": "spriteFrame", "value": "sprite-uuid-here"}}

⚠️ IMPORTANT: 1) Get UUIDs from asset_query and node_query tools first! 2) Use component_query to inspect exact property types - type mismatches will cause failures!
